Version 0.5.9-ko:

- Added default-on DS/DSi Touch Menu controls for menus and the ROM/File
  Chooser with Bottom Screen routing, edge/release debounce, visible-row hit
  testing, select-before-activate safety, scrolling, and full physical-control
  compatibility.
- Implemented MBC7 dual access enables, sensor latching, serial EEPROM
  read/write/erase/all commands, persistence, and versioned transaction state.
- Corrected HuC1 RAM/IR selection and independent ROM/RAM banking. Added
  portable MBC7 and HuC1 tests while leaving physical validation explicit.
- Expanded WX per-line hide/resume and SGB packet boundary tests and documented
  exact incomplete SGB host CPU/APU/DSP coverage.
- Raised save-state version to 8, made release-note selection explicit in the
  deterministic packager, and retained loading of older states.

Version 0.5.8-ko:

- Added independent MMM01 support for cartridge types 0x0B, 0x0C, and 0x0D,
  including the unmapped menu banks, mapping enable, ROM/RAM masks, mode lock,
  multiplex banking, SRAM/autosave, and versioned save-state restoration.
- Reclassified legacy cartridge types 0x15-0x17 as undocumented/unknown and
  stopped silently falling back to MBC5. MBC7/HuC hardware behavior was not
  changed or claimed as validated.
- Added an isolated SGB host runtime foundation with bounded SNES WRAM and PPU
  registers, a deliberately faulting 65C816 subset, an SPC700/APU transfer and
  execution subset, BRR voice decoding, prototype OBJ decoding, and separate
  DS host-audio PCM output.
- Connected DATA_SND, DATA_TRN, JUMP, SOUND, SOU_TRN, CHR_TRN, and prototype
  OBJ_TRN to the host runtime while preserving the existing SGB palette,
  attribute, border, mask, multiplayer, and PAL priority paths.
- Raised save-state version to 7 and explicitly serialized MMM01 and SGB host
  state while retaining loading support for earlier state versions.
- Added portable MMM01 and SGB host regression tests. Full host-SNES CPU/APU
  coverage and final prototype OBJ composition remain tracked work and are not
  represented as complete.

Version 0.5.7-ko:

- Added the new GameYob project logo and derived a 16-color DS/DSi banner icon
  from the same artwork.
- Refocused the default release on `gameyob.nds` and `gameyob_dsi.nds`, both of
  which can be used on supported DS-family launchers and Nintendo 3DS DS mode.
- Preserved the exact published `v0.5.5-ko` native 3DSX executable under
  `backup/3dsx`, moved its detailed follow-up work into a dedicated TODO, and
  changed native 3DS CI to an explicit manual workflow.
- Made native 3DSX inclusion optional in the deterministic packager. The
  `v0.5.7-ko` archive contains DS/DSi binaries, multilingual guides, language
  examples, checksums, and license notices, but no ROM, BIOS, or 3DSX file.
- Updated the English, Japanese, and Korean user guides and reorganized the
  main TODO around the remaining DS/DSi validation and compatibility work.

Version 0.5.5-ko:

- Migrated the Nintendo DS and DSi builds to the pinned BlocksDS 1.22.2 SDK
  and Wonderful toolchain while retaining a separate current libctru/devkitARM
  build for native Nintendo 3DS.
- Added embedded English, Japanese, and Korean menus with UTF-8 custom language
  files in INI, JSON, XML, and YAML formats. Saving settings can create a
  non-destructive English language template.
- Completed UTF-8/CP949 Korean ROM filename, path, and cheat-list handling on
  DS, DSi, and native 3DS, including UTF-16-to-UTF-8 3DS directory conversion.
- Added native 3DS LAN link discovery and host/client play with protocol
  versioning, ROM fingerprints, CRC, sequence numbers, ACK/retry,
  fragmentation, input buffering, state hashes, timeouts, and initial SRAM/RTC
  synchronization.
- Hardened DS/DSi NiFi and local-link restart behavior, secondary save
  isolation, cross-ROM setup, bounds checks, and offline/no-peer return paths.
- Stabilized MBC3 and HuC3 RTC behavior, including latch edges, halt, day carry,
  backward host-clock handling, RTC-only cartridges, saves, and save states.
- Hardened patched-ROM support using physical file length, safe
  non-power-of-two bank mirroring, partial-bank fill, standard SRAM sizes up to
  128 KiB, and an explicit 8 MiB MBC5 boundary.
- Fixed DMG sprite ordering, horizontal Window clipping, LCD-off output, CGB
  background priority, noise-channel LFSR behavior, and additional SGB command
  and border state handling.
- Added selectable 0x900-byte GBC BIOS paths on DS, DSi, and native 3DS, stored
  as `biosfile` in `gameyobds.ini`.
- Updated native 3DS audio to prefer hardware CSND with NDSP fallback and added
  debug status for the active audio backend.
- Native 3DS ROM operation was accepted on real hardware with a fixed centered
  160x144 display. Occasional frame drops remain. Unstable native 3DS scaling
  was removed from this release and deferred to the v0.5.6-ko target; DS/DSi
  scaling remains available.
- Added English, Japanese, and Korean user guides, deterministic release
  packaging, SHA-256 checksums, and complete redistributed license notices.

Version 0.5.3-ko:

- Added Korean UTF-8/CP949 ROM filenames, directory names, cheat names, and
  related save, state, and printer paths.
- Added native Nintendo 3DS Super Game Boy border decoding and display.
- Fixed DMG sprite ordering, horizontal Window clipping, LCD-off white output,
  CGB background priority, and 15-bit/7-bit noise-channel LFSR behavior.
- Added DS/DSi NiFi protocol v2 bounds checks, versioning, sequencing,
  checksums, ROM identity, retransmission, input buffering, state hashes, and
  initial SRAM transfer.
- Added reproducible Nintendo DS, Nintendo DSi, and Nintendo 3DS CI builds.

Version 0.5.2-ko.1:

- Added Korean filename and cheat-list text support to the v0.5.2 homebrew
  release while preserving the original emulator license and release layout.

Version 0.5:

- Added Gameboy Printer emulation
- Added GBS playback feature
- Added "scale" button
- Semi-overhauled menu: now colorized, and does not interrupt emulation.
- Improved Super Gameboy emulation
- Selectable custom borders
- Reduced autosaving lag (results may vary between flashcards and SD cards)
- Implemented the halt bug (fixes The Smurfs)
- Wram register has unused bits set (fixes Metal Gear Solid)
- More fixes to emulation accuracy, sound, etc
- Stability fixes (most notably for sleep mode), many other minor bugfixes

Version 0.4.1:

- Fixed "save" button (which was bugged) and reduced autosaving lag

Version 0.4:

- New Icon by Corbin Davenport
- Implemented Super Gameboy support
- Implemented scaling (for those who don't like borders)
- Implemented custom borders (for those who don't like scaling)
- Implemented autosaving (causes lag in some games; off by default)
- Added "Detect GBA" option to access the advance shop in the Oracle games
- Added Fast Forward toggle button
- Added "Sound Fix" option for very accurate sound timing; it may use more power.
- Added Rumble Pak Support for Ez-3in1 and Warioware Twisted carts (thanks to windwakr)
- Added support for Gameshark and Game Genie codes (thanks to LemonBoy)
- Support for Rockman 8, HuC1/HuC3 mappers and Robopon games (thanks to LemonBoy)
- Second screen's backlight is disabled when not needed to save power
- (partial) Stereo sound emulation
- More improvements to emulation & sound accuracy

Version 0.3:

- Surpasses Lameboy in speed by about 10 FPS, thanks to optimizations by Nebuleon and myself
- Added fast forward mode (courtesy of Nebuleon)
- Added support for many exotic graphical effects & fixed screen-change graphical bugs
- Added MBC2 support (for Kid Icarus, Final Fantasy Adventure)
- Added save states and suspending (temporary states)
- Added option to save settings to gameyob.ini
- Added HIGHLY EXPERIMENTAL NiFi link cable emulation (works with Tetris, Dr. Mario, and Pokemon if you're lucky)
- Fixed various emulation bugs, increasing compatibility
- Fixed many causes of crashes (DSi mode works now)
- Soft resetting works (L+R+Start+Select)
- 100% remappable controls
- Sound bugfixes

Version 0.2:

- Fixed some sound emulation bugs
- Fixed sleep-mode crashes
- Fixed window behaviour when modified mid-frame (fixes text in Resident Evil Gaiden)
- Fixed interrupt behaviour (fixes boss intros in Megaman V & passes blargg's cpu test #2)
- Fixed crashes in some games without sram (Avenging Spirit)
- Set default # of ram banks to 4 (workaround for Japanese Crystal)
- Added GBC Bios support
- Added "B/Y" control option
- Added a little clock
- Capitalized rom extensions are detected properly

Version 0.1.2:

- Fixed Z flag for sla (hl) and rl (hl) opcodes

Version 0.1.1:

- Removed limit on number of files per directory
